{"seq":14,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:13:18.339Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"36c976b192d8b17f384d1b6dea53b43118f99f85d170176276fac35eac306690","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Hollis. I went through every Moss note I can see in the shared files. There are two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct got through the gate normally.\n2. *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also logged by Thea: gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The note doesn't say whether it was ever resolved.\n\nSome other numbers might get mixed up with these:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in Moss's Central notes, but they're for Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not QFL.\n• Moss's other QFL notes (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in) have no ticket numbers.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one R) is about a different company, which isn't a customer.\n\nI only checked the shared notes and digests. I didn't look at the account's CRM or ticket system, so there could be QFL tickets Moss never wrote down."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-h2h-2026-11/zero-lean-opus-none-mu-v03-dev2/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T07:13:24.041Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"6664010cd48601377a82948cb2d6088fb36269f2655172e044abf8ecc03a7bc6","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I've sent you the list in our DM. Moss's notes mention two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" note dated 5 Oct 2025. Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025: drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments from the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and the next morning's 04:00 shift got through the gate normally.\n2. **#4419**, from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet\". Thea also logged this one: gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The note doesn't say whether it was ever fixed.\n\nSome numbers could get mixed up with these, so I left them out:\n- **#4409, #4412 and FR-882** are in Moss's Central notes, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply.\n- **\"Quarendon Freightways\"** (spelled with one R) comes up in one of Marcus's notes. It's a different company and not a customer.\n\nMoss's other two Quarrendon notes, the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in, have no ticket numbers in them. I only checked the shared notes, not the CRM or the ticket system, so there may be other Quarrendon tickets Moss never wrote down."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
